; Part of millgui. MIT licence, see millgui/LICENSE.
; FIND single edge (millgui's RIGHT EDGE). The probe starts at probing depth
; beside the right face, within #3018 of it, and moves -X to touch
; it once (o<millgui_edge>: fast touch, back off #3019, slow touch). The
; edge is the contact minus the effective tip radius #5410 / 2 - #3032 and
; is reported as x_minus_probed_position / #1005. With #3030 = 0
; the active work offset's X is set so that the edge reads 0; no other
; axis is written. No Z motion. Ends #3019 off the face at the same Z, with
; the modal state as it was.
o<probe_x_minus_wco> sub
o10 if [#<_task> EQ 0]
    o<probe_x_minus_wco> return
o10 endif
o<millgui_probe_ready> call
M73
M50 P0
G90 G94
o<millgui_edge> call [0] [-1] [#3018]
o20 if [#3030 EQ 0]
    G10 L20 P0 X[#5420 - #<_millgui_edge>]
o20 endif
o<probe_x_minus_wco> endsub
M2
